  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a shared target pathway with Thrombopoietin, as it is involved in the regulation of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets Thrombopoietin. This suggests that Mollicellin N may influence the activity of this compound, potentially modulating the production of Thrombopoietin. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship, with Mollicellin N acting as a mediator in the signaling cascade leading to Thrombopoietin. The presence of multiple targets along this pathway, including A704 and Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, further supports the idea that Mollicellin N is part of a broader regulatory network that affects Thrombopoietin. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to play a role in the biological processes that regulate Thrombopoietin, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
